I go back to my table.
My seat by the window is very nice.
I look out the window.
Outside it is still extremely cold.
The people on the street are freezing.
They are all walking very fast.
In here it is wonderfully warm.
I open my backpack.
I take out my mobile phone.
I have three new messages.
They are from my sister Sofia in Mexico.
I read her messages.
The weather in Mexico is very sunny today.
I smile and write a short reply.
A little later, the waiter comes to my table.
He brings my order.
"Here is your large coffee," he says.
"And here is the chocolate cake."
"Thank you very much," I say politely.
"You're very welcome."
"Enjoy!" he replies.
